1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Al-Sayyida Nafīsa (Arabic: سيدة نفيسة) (b. 145/762 – d. 208/824)was the daughter of al-Hasan al-Anwar, the son of Zayd, son of Imam al-Hasan (a). She was buried in Cairo, Egypt. In historical books,she is well-know
2 CONC n for her worship, asceticism, narrating hadith, generosity and memorizing Qur'an. She was married to Ishaq al-Mu'tamin, the son of Imam al-Sadiq (a). Al-Sayyida Nafisa mausoleum is among the most visited sites of Muslims, especia
2 CONC lly for the Egyptian Shi'a.
2 CONT
