2 CONT Jump to navigationJump to search Yahya ibn Umar ibn Yahya ibn Husayn ibn Zayd ibn Ali Zayn al-Abidin ibn Al-Husayn ibn Ali[1] was an Alid Imam. His mother was Umm al-Husayn Fatimah bint al-Husayn ibn Abdallah ibn Ismail ibn Abdull
2 CONC ah ibn Ja`far ibn Abī Tālib. [2] In the days of the Abbasid Caliph Al-Musta'in, he marched out from Kufa and lead an abortive uprising from Kufa in 250 A.H. (864-65 C.E.),[3] but was killed by the Abbasid forces led by Hussain ibn
2 CONC  Isma’il, who had been sent to deal with him.... ...
