1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT 33eme generation
2 CONT Abu Jafar Mohammad ol-Akbar
2 CONT ================
2 CONT Allameh Qutb Ravandi
2 CONT
2 CONT In 573 AH, Allameh    Qutbuddin Ravandi,   one of the brilliant figures of the Shiite world, passed away. Ravandi, a great   sixth-century scientist, has also trained   prominent students, including ...  Ali ibn   Muhammad al -Ma'
2 CONC idani,  
2 CONT
2 CONT [... ancestor of Seid Javad Hosseini Khamenei [https://www.geni.com/people/Seyyed-Javad-Khamenei/6000000049379572971] is from the Sadat Aftasi dynasty. [11] His lineage goes back to Sultan Seyyed Ahmad, who is the fourth leader of
2 CONC  the Shiites through five intermediaries of Sajjad's descendants . [12] [13] [14] Among his other ancestors, we can mention Sultan Sayyid Muhammad, who reached Ali ibn Hussein (Zayn al-Abidin) through four intermediaries. [15]
2 CONT
2 CONT =====================
2 CONT
2 CONT [Seyyed Mohammad migrated from Medina to the central regions of Iran and Tafresh, Ashtian and Farahan, but was arrested and killed by Abbasi agents in Tafresh . His grave is in Miqan, Arak ](https://fa.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D8%B3%DB
2 CONC %8C%D8%AF_%D8%AC%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%AF_%D8%AE%D8%A7%D9%85%D9%86%D9%87%E2%80%8C%D8%A7%DB%8C) Seyyed Mohammad est le maillon qui vous relie, non pas au 9ème Imam (al-Jawad)comme je pensais, mais au 4ème Imam, Ali Zayn al-Abidin (as), vi
2 CONC a son fils Ali al-Asghar.
