1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Zahir was born around 1690.[5][b] His father, Umar, was a sheikh of the Banu Zaydan, a small family of Bedouin (nomadic Arab) origin which had abandoned nomadism under Zahir's grandfather, Salih,[c]
2 CONT
2 CONT  The name of Zahir's grandfather, who was not mentioned directly in the contemporary sources, was confirmed in a mosque inscription found in the Galilee village of Damun dated to 1722 or 1723, which credited Zahir's uncle, 'Ali ib
2 CONC n Salih', as its builder.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sharon, M. (2004). Corpus Inscriptionum Arabicarum Palaestinae, D-F. Brill. ISBN 978-90-04-13197-2.
