2 CONT Zahir had five wives during his lifetime.[107] Among his wives was a woman from the Sardiyah, a Bedouin tribe active in Transjordan and Palestine.[108] Zahir was also married to a daughter of Sayyid Muhammad, a wealthy religious n
2 CONC otable from Damascus,[10] a daughter of the mukhtar (headman) of Bi'ina,[13] and a daughter of the mukhtar of Deir al-Qassi.[19]
