1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Zayadina
2 CONT The Zayadina expanded their iltizam and territory over much of the Galilee during the 1730s, with Sa'd's younger brother, Zahir al-Umar, emerging as the family's preeminent chief. He took over the town of Tiberias, gained its ilti
2 CONC zam, and fortified it as his headquarters starting around 1730. Sa'd moved the family seat from Arraba to nearby Deir Hanna, which he considerably fortified. Their cousin Muhammad, the son of their uncle Ali, continued to dominate
2 CONC  the area of Shefa-Amr from his father's headquarters in Damun. By 1740, Zahir and the family had gained the iltizam or otherwise imposed their control in Safed and its environs, Nazareth, the fortress of Jiddin and the coastal pl
2 CONC ain of Acre, and the fortress villages of Bi'ina in the Shaghur,[10] Deir al-Qassi, and Suhmata.[11]
