1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT the first 'Bilgrami'
2 CONT
2 CONT Syed Dawood came from Wast and Syed Zaidi al Wast started in Bilgram with him. He was a murid (disciple) of Khwaja Bhaktiar Khaki (the Sufi mystic who started the Phoolwalon ki Sayr festival near Delhi) and was close to Sultan Sha
2 CONC msuddin Altamash. He used Khwaja's mediation to obtain approval to take over Bilgram. He attacked and defeated Raja Siri, who was aided by Raja Kanauj (AH614 / 1217 AD).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bilgram was earlier called Sirinagar. New name derived from a Yogi from Siri called Bel. (Gram=village). The stay in Bilgram marked by Chronogram 'Khuda Dad' in 614AH or 1217AD.)
