1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad Sahib Mirbat (https://www.geni.com/people/Muhammad-Sahib-Mirbat/6000000001489779696?through=6000000184645632165) has 2 recorded sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alawi 'Am al-Faqih' (Uncle of the jurist) https://www.geni.com/people/Alawi-Am-al-Faqih/6000000184645632165
2 CONT Ali 'Walid al-Faqih' (father of the jurist). https://www.geni.com/people/Ali-Walid-al-Faqih/6000000219887508954
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_al-Faqih_al-Muqaddam
2 CONT
2 CONT >[https://www.geni.com/people/Muhammad-al-Faqih-al-Muqaddam/6000000002956981502?through=6000000219887508954 '''Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī Bā ʿAlawī'''] (Arabic: محمد بن علي باعلوي) commonly known as al-Faqīh al-Muqaddam, 574 H - 653 H or 1
2 CONC 178 CE - 1232 CE) is known as the founder of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ba_%27Alawiyya Ba 'Alawiyya] Sufi order[1], which has influenced Sufism in Yemen, South Asia and Southeast Asia. He is the only son of '''Ali''' son of ''
2 CONC 'Muhammad Sahib al-Mirbath''' whom all 75 families of Ba 'Alawi sada that spread out from Yemen to Southeast Asia are rooted.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~naqobatulasyrof/family/main/des/d17.htm#i9
2 CONT
2 CONT 65. ALI-MUH.SHOHIB.MARBAT-17 (MUHAMMAD.SHOHIB.MARBAT-1662, Ali.Kholi AL-GOSAM-1560, ALWI-MUHAMMAD-1459, MUHAMMAD-ALWI-1358, ALWI-UBAIDILLAH-1254, ABDULLAH.UBAIDILLAH-1151, AHMAD.ALMUHAJIR-1049, ISA.ARUMI-940, MUHAMMAD.ANAGIB-835, 
2 CONC ALI*AL-UREIDHI-730, JA'FAR*ASSADIQ-625, MUHAMMAD.ALBAGIR-514, ALI.ZAINALABIDIN-45, SAIDINA*HUSSEIN-ALI-ABITHOLIB-3(RA)4, FATIMAH.AZZAHRA-2(RAH)2, Unknown1) died in 590h In Tarim, Yemen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: birth date unknown. Ali died 590H in Tarim, Yemen.
2 CONT Ali became the father of Muhammad Al-faqih Al-muqaddam in Trim, Hadhramut, 574H. Ali bin Muhammad Sahib Mirbaat was an eminent scholar, a great Sufi saint and extremely humble. He died in Tarym in 590H, and had only one son, Muham
2 CONC mad better known as Al Faqih Al Muqadam, the greatest professor -Muhammad bin Ali.
2 CONT
2 CONT ALI-MUH.SHOHIB.MARBAT-17 married (name unknown). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 69 M    i. Muhammad AL.FAGIH.ALMUGADAM-ALI-18 was born in 574h-Tarim, Hadramaut and died in 653h-Tarim, Hadhramut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ar.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%85%D8%AF_%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%AD%D8%A8_%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B7
2 CONT
2 CONT states he has 4 sons and being the eldest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Keturunan 
2 CONT sunting 
2 CONT Syeikh Muhammad Shahib Mirbath dilahirkan di kota Tarim, Yaman. Beliau telah dikurniai empat orang anak lelaki, iaitu Abdullah, Ahmad, Alwi dan Ali. Abdullah dan Ahmad tidak menurunkan keturunan, sedangkan Alwi dan Ali menjadi cik
2 CONC al-bakal keturunan para Sayyid dari kaum Alawiyyin (Habaib), termasuk yang berada di kawasan Asia Tenggara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dua orang putera Sayyid Muhammad bin Ali yang yang menjadi pangkal keturunan kepada semua golongan Sayyid kaum Alawiyin ialah:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ali 
2 CONT Muhammad, yang bergelar al-A'dham al-Faqih al-Muqaddam 
2 CONT Alwi Ami al-Faqih, yang terkenal dengan sebutan `Ammul al-Faqih al-Muqaddam. 
2 CONT Abdulmalik[2] 
2 CONT Abdullah[2] 
2 CONT Ali[3] 
2 CONT Abdurrahman[2] 
2 CONT Ahmad[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ghayb.com/muhammad-al-faqih-al-muqaddam-the-ba-alawiyya-order/
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage and Early Life
2 CONT Noble Genealogy
2 CONT Muhammad al-Faqih al-Muqaddam belongs to one of the most distinguished lineages in Islamic history, tracing his ancestry directly to the Prophet Muhammad through his daughter Fatimah and son-in-law Ali ibn Abi Talib215. This noble
2 CONC  genealogy, meticulously preserved and documented in numerous historical texts, connects him to the Ahl al-Bayt (the Prophet’s household) and establishes his position as a Sayyid, a title of respect given to descendants of the Pro
2 CONC phet315. His patrilineal lineage, as recorded in various sources, follows this path: Muhammad (al-Faqih al-Muqaddam), son of ''Ali'', son of Muhammad Sahib al-Mirbat, son of Ali Khali’ Qasam, son of Alawi, son of Muhammad Sahib al
2 CONC -Sawma’ah, son of Alawi, son of Ubaydullah, son of Ahmad al-Muhajir, son of Isa, son of Muhammad al-Naqib, son of Ali al-Uraydi, son of Ja’far al-Sadiq, son of Muhammad al-Baqir, son of Ali Zayn al-Abidin, son of Husayn, son of Al
2 CONC i ibn Abi Talib and Fatimah al-Zahra, daughter of Prophet Muhammad2316.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
