1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Menurunkan keturunan al-Qadri.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://freepages.family.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~naqobatulasyrof/main/des/d23.htm#i95
2 CONT
2 CONT was born in Tarim, Hadhramut 750H. Muhammad died 845H in Tarim, Hadhramut, at 95 years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Habib Saleh traces his lineage back to the great servant of Allah and famous divine Al Imam Muhammad Jamali-lleyl (750H - 845H) bin Hassan Al Mualim. This is the Imam who was the first to be called Jamali-lleyl, which has two mean
2 CONC ings, The first meaning - 'the Night Camel' infered to his night services of visiting all the mosques of Tarim with his camel, when every body was asleep, pouring water from the wells into the big ports for the early morning praye
2 CONC r. The second interpretation of the meaning of Jamali-lleyl was inferred to him metaphorically as he beautified his night in the service of God, in prayers, meditation and reciting of the Holy Qur'an till down. Persistency in his 
2 CONC commitments was one of his remarkable qualities. Muhammad Jamalleyl is also known as Muhammad Shayba, meaning Muhammad the Old man, as he had a long life and died at the age of 95.He is also known as Muhammad Sahib Rawghah, meanin
2 CONC g the owner of Rawghah, a location outside Tarim where he was residing and built his own Mosque called 'Jamali-llyyl Mosque.
2 CONT
2 CONT He counts two eminent Imams among his students, namely Al Qutb Abdalla bin Abubakar Al Idarus, the author of Al kibryt al Ahmar, and al Qutb Ali bin Abubakar Al Sakran (from the love of Allah), the author of al Barqatul Mashiqa, a
2 CONC n invaluable treatise of Tariqa Ala Baalawy (Order of Ala Baalawy), May Allah be pleased with them all. He had two children, Ali and Abdalla.
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad Jamaly-lleyl had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 100 i. Abdallah23 Jamaly-lleyl.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 101 ii. Ali Jamaly-lleyl.
