2 CONT Ahmed Ben Bella (Arabic: أحمد بن بلّة, romanized: Aḥmad bin Billah; 25 December 1916 – 11 April 2012) was an Algerian politician, soldier and revolutionary who served as the head of government of Algeria from 27 September 1962 to 
2 CONC 15 September 1963 and then the first president of Algeria from 15 September 1963 until his overthrow on 19 June 1965.
